as savings or dividend income depending on the fund's nature. Distributions are not taxed again; the reportable income figure already covers them.\n\n**Disposal gains** are taxed as chargeable gains under Capital Gains Tax, not income. To prevent double taxation, the reportable income you were taxed on is added to your base cost, which reduces the gain on sale. Gains are subject to the CGT annual exempt amount and the current CGT rates.\n\nNote that losses on a reporting fund are treated as capital losses, not income losses, so they can only offset capital gains.","ttft_ms":4683,"type":"result","duration_ms":5983,"uuid":"b96789dc-5449-4c72-8cc7-9df8ea73e53d","ttft_stream_ms":795,"time_to_request_ms":67,"first_content_frame_ms":795,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
